# Services & API

## Domain folder shape

Each domain under [`app/services/<domain>/`](mdc:app/services/):

```
api/*.api.ts      # CRUD class, requests via useApi
types/*.types.ts  # + types/index.ts
helpers/*.helper.js
index.ts          # re-export api + types + helpers
```

## Calling the API

- Use [`useApi`](mdc:app/composables/useApi.js) from a CRUD class. `useFetch` runs in component setup and returns `{ data, loading, error }`
- Do **not** use `$fetch` / `apiFetch` for Nest API calls
- Call CRUD methods during `<script setup>` with no `await`, so `loading` stays reactive and SSR waits for the request
- Later calls (filters, next page, submit) go through `nuxtApp.runWithContext(() => Crud.method(...))`
- Pass `cache: false` when the same payload must hit the network again (creates, explicit reloads)
- Public catalog paths stay `/app-api`. This app has no auth token and does not send `organization_id`
- Client requests use a relative URL so Nitro proxies `/app-api`. Server requests use `runtimeConfig.public.baseUrl`

```ts
// ✅
export class TeachersCrud {
  static get(params = {}) {
    const { request } = useApi();
    const { data, pending, error, ...rest } = request({
      endpoint: "/app-api/teachers",
      method: "GET",
      params,
    });
    return { data, error, loading: pending, ...rest };
  }
}

// component setup
const { data, loading, error } = TeachersCrud.get();

// ❌ await $fetch / apiFetch inside onMounted
```

## Helpers vs UI

- Form mapping / list normalize / query builders → `helpers/*.helper.js`
- Keep Vue components thin: call service exports, don’t embed endpoint paths
